    "stay_on_level_after_submit": "false",
    "teacher_markdown": "**Strong:** Says no, and explains that this is a live, individual record — one specific resident’s application status — not a stable fact the system could have been given ahead of time. Explicitly connects this to the library chatbot’s holiday gap: both are cases where the system would confidently answer something it was never actually given data for.\r\n\r\n**Partial:** Says no with reasonable individual-case reasoning (“every application is different,” “this changes day to day”) but doesn’t explicitly link it back to the library example, or the connection is vague (“AI can make mistakes”).\r\n\r\n**Weak:** Says yes, it’s fine to trust without review — or gives a reason unrelated to the live-data distinction (e.g., “chatbots are always risky,” or a generic statement that doesn’t explain why this particular question is the risky one compared to the others)."
